#N canvas 40 60 1100 700 12;
#X text 20 10 [nn.softmax] - turn a list of scores into probabilities that add up to 1, f 120;
#X text 20 31 p[i] = exp(score[i] / T) / sum of all exp(score[j] / T). The TEMPERATURE T decides how sharp the choice is: small T = the best score takes (almost) everything \, large T = everything gets a similar share. Softmax is the heart of attention in transformers and of how language models pick the next word., f 120;
#X text 20 82 ARGUMENTS: 1) array with the scores 2) array for the probabilities (same size). LEFT INLET: bang = compute. RIGHT INLET: temperature (default 1). OUTLET: bang when ready. The largest score is subtracted first so exp() can never overflow - real implementations do the same., f 120;
